OL,3,GNEWSAHistoric ferry service secured for
OL,4,Aanother year
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 180-year-old river ferry crossing
OL,7,Fwill continue for another year after
OL,8,Fcouncillors agreed additional funding.
OL,10,FThe Fleetwood-Knott End ferry service
OL,11,Fconnects the two towns either side of
OL,12,Fthe River Wyre estuary and carries up
OL,13,Fto 35 people.
OL,15,FLancashire County Council (LCC) is
OL,16,Fresponsible for the running costs but
OL,17,Fshares them equally with Wyre Council
OL,18,Funder an agreement.
OL,20,FLCC previously committed #57,110 a year
OL,21,Ftowards the service and has now agreed
OL,22,Fto provide a further #62,000.
